WELL {WELL_ID}

THE TASK IN QUESTION:
{TASK}

OTHER LATE TASKS ON THIS WELL PLANNED TO FINISH BEFORE THIS ONE STARTS (nearest first; timing only - the data holds no dependency links):
{EARLIER_LATE_TASKS}

OTHER LATE TASKS IN THE SAME WBS:
{SAME_WBS_LATE_TASKS}

{MILESTONES}

ASSIGNED CREW (crew_id {ASSIGNED_CREW_ID}) - ITS WORKLOAD ACROSS THE FLEET:
{ASSIGNED_CREW}

AVAILABLE CREWS OF THIS TYPE (crew_type_id {CREW_TYPE_ID}): {AVAILABLE_COUNT} available, {BUSY_COUNT} busy, of {TYPE_TOTAL}. The best candidates - name ONLY these:
{AVAILABLE_CREWS}

{NOTE}

Answer both questions now, as the JSON.

WELL {WELL_ID}

{MILESTONES}

TASK TALLY (latest record per task):
{TASK_TALLY}

LATE WORK BY WBS (worst first):
{LATE_BY_WBS}

LATE WORK BY CREW TYPE - with the assigned crews' fleet load and the best FREE crews of the same type (name ONLY these candidates, under their own type):
{LATE_BY_CREW_TYPE}

MOST URGENT LATE TASKS (most urgent first):
{MOST_URGENT}

{NOTE}

Answer both questions now, as the JSON.

Report date: {REPORT_DATE}

Tools:
{TOOLS}

Question: {QUESTION}

Report date: {REPORT_DATE}
Question: {QUESTION}

Tool results (authoritative):
{TOOL_RESULTS}

Your previous draft was rejected by the verifier for these reasons:
{ISSUES}

Previous draft:
{DRAFT}

Write a corrected answer that fixes every issue.

You check a draft answer against the tool results it was written from. You do not rewrite it.

Return ONLY a JSON object: {"ok": true|false, "issues": ["<short issue>", ...]}

Report an issue only when the draft:
- states a figure, date or well id that is not in the tool results;
- states a cause, a blame, or a judgement (late, delayed, at risk) the results do not give;
- contradicts a tool result;
- presents a crew as an assignment rather than an advisory mention.
Wording, style and length are not issues.

Tool results:
{TOOL_RESULTS}

Draft:
{DRAFT}

unknown_tool: unknown tool {TOOL}
required: '{NAME}' is required
whole_number: '{NAME}' must be a whole number, got {VALUE}
one_of: '{NAME}' must be one of {OPTIONS}
no_task: no task with task_daily_id {TASK_DAILY_ID} on {REPORT_DATE}
failed: the tool failed: {DETAIL}

Respond with ONLY this JSON, no prose and no markdown. Every value is a string:
{"proposals": [{"title": "", "what_is_wrong": "", "why_it_matters": "", "how_to_detect": "", "do_not_flag": "", "category": "", "severity": "critical|high|medium|low", "entity": "", "evidence": "", "observation_id": "OBS-nnn", "confidence": "high|medium|low"}]}
When nothing is worth a person's time, reply {"proposals": []}.

TABLE INDEX (every table in scope, with its column names):
{TABLE_INDEX}

THE RULE TO GROUND:
{RULE}

Which of these tables does this rule concern? Reply with the JSON.

STARTING POINT - a previous version of this probe. Treat it as a draft, not as truth: verify every table and column against the SCHEMA block above, and correct anything that has been renamed, retyped or removed. Keep its intent, fix its facts.

SUMMARY:
{SEED_SUMMARY}

DETAIL:
{SEED_DETAIL}

YOUR PREVIOUS ATTEMPT WAS:

SUMMARY:
{SUMMARY_SQL}

DETAIL:
{DETAIL_SQL}

{PREVIOUS}

IT WAS REJECTED BEFORE IT RAN:
{ERROR}

{PREVIOUS}

IT FAILED WHEN RUN. The database reported:
{ERROR}
Fix it - check the table and column names, the joins and the types against the SCHEMA block above.

{PREVIOUS}

IT RAN, BUT WHAT IT RETURNED CANNOT BE USED:
{ERROR}

{PREVIOUS}

AN INDEPENDENT REVIEWER REJECTED IT.
WHAT TO FIX:
{FEEDBACK}

THE PROBE AS WRITTEN:
SUMMARY QUERY:
{SUMMARY_SQL}

DETAIL QUERY:
{DETAIL_SQL}

WHAT IT RETURNED WHEN RUN.
Summary row (one row by contract - these counts are the truth):
{SUMMARY_ROW}

Detail sample (at most {SAMPLE_ROWS} rows, for judging the SHAPE of the result - never count or rank from it):
{DETAIL_SAMPLE}

YOU ALREADY REJECTED AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS PROBE, SAYING:
{HISTORY}

The author has acted on that. Do NOT now ask for the opposite of what you asked for before - if your earlier instruction was wrong, say so plainly in the feedback and give the corrected instruction ONCE. If the author did what you asked and the probe is now sound, APPROVE it.

WHAT EACH CHECK FOUND, worst first:
severity | records affected | of examined | share | what was found
{ROWS}
